Subject: [PATCH] a2dp: clear the last used pair when its remote SEP is freed

chan->last_used keeps a pointer to a remote SEP. When a Discover drops a
cached SEP the remote no longer reports (remove_disappeared), the pointer was
left dangling and a2dp_find_eps() dereferenced it. Free the pair together with
the SEP. Not specific to this firmware: a candidate for upstream.

diff -ruN a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
--- a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
+++ b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
@@ -1858,6 +1858,13 @@
 
 	avdtp_remote_sep_set_destroy(sep->sep, NULL, NULL);
 
+	/* The last used pair points at this remote SEP: forget it, or
+	 * a2dp_find_eps() reads freed memory once a rediscovery drops it. */
+	if (sep->chan->last_used && sep->chan->last_used->rsep == sep) {
+		free(sep->chan->last_used);
+		sep->chan->last_used = NULL;
+	}
+
 	free(sep->path);
 	free(sep);
 }
